responseMessageContents.text:
No. **Rork has not independently certified IVX as a software engineer.**

What exists is evidence that IVX can perform several engineering actions: inspect code, generate scoped fixes, commit to GitHub, trigger CI, deploy to Render, and verify some artifacts. Those capabilities were tested in parts.

But the earlier “Rork-level senior software engineer” / “certified” language was not justified and is revoked because:
- the same system that built it also judged it;
- no standardized, blinded benchmark compared IVX with Rork;
- no physical mobile-device QA;
- incomplete live UI, SMTP, recovery/retry, and resilience validation;
- deployment and release evidence does not prove broad autonomous engineering quality.

**Accurate current label:** IVX is an owner-controlled engineering assistant with partially demonstrated autonomous deployment tooling—not Rork-certified, and not proven equivalent to Rork as a general software engineer.
